# Tools the CI gate checks for on a venue before it runs this suite.
#
# The list is DERIVED from the suite by ci-gate.sh (it reads the spawn calls in
# test/ and reports zip, tar, gpg, ssh and pnpm). This file only CORRECTS that
# derivation: a bare name adds a tool the scan cannot see, a leading `-` drops a
# false positive.
#
# unzip is reached one level down, which is why the scan misses it. The release
# smoke runs sign.sh, whose pre-sign dev-mock gate
# (tools/build-reproduce/check-no-dev-mock.sh) unpacks the staged extension zip,
# and the scan does not follow a shell script the suite executes through bash.
# `zip` missing from a CI runner on 2026-08-06 is what surfaced this gap; `unzip`
# is the same gap one call deeper. tar needs no line here: the suite spawns it directly.
unzip
# ditto is a FALSE POSITIVE from the scan (row 144). It is Apple's own
# archiver, it exists only on macOS, and every call to it in
# release-launch-probe.smoke.js sits behind a `process.platform === 'darwin'`
# guard - the Linux venue drives the AppImage lane instead and never spawns it.
# Demanding it would make the suite unrunnable on every Linux venue in the pool
# to satisfy a call none of them reaches.
-ditto
